<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Corrective Move</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1969</span> · Also known as Corrective Step</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Corrective Move was the seizure of power on 22 June 1969 by the left wing of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-yemen">South Yemen</a>'s ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a>, which removed President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qahtan-al-shaabi">Qahtan al-Shaabi</a>. Power passed to a collective leadership including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salim-rubaya-ali">Salim Rubaya Ali</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdul-fattah-ismail">Abdul Fattah Ismail</a>, which renamed the country the People's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-republic-of-yemen">Democratic Republic of Yemen</a> in 1970 and aligned it with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> as the Arab world's only Marxist state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/corrective-move.jpg" alt="Corrective Move" width="233" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Corrective_Move_PDR_Yemen_postage_stamp.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
